# Vista (OpenDriveLab/Vista commit cc9821b4, docs/INSTALL.md: Python 3.9, PyTorch 2.0.1, CUDA 11.7) requirements.txt,
# the inference subset that sample.py / sample_utils.py / train.py (top-level imports only) and vwm/ import on the sampling
# path, at the versions pinned there; open ">=" pins are resolved as of the weights release (2024-06-07, --exclude-newer).
# Not listed here (training, data, logging or demo-UI code only; not imported on the sampling path the adapter uses):
# black, chardet, clip (openai), deepspeed, fairscale, fire, invisible-watermark, ninja, opencv-python, pandas, pudb,
# streamlit, tensorboardx, torchaudio, torchdata, wandb, webdataset. timm, torchmetrics, urllib3 and wheel still come in as
# dependencies of open-clip-torch / pytorch-lightning / requests. triton 2.0.0 comes with torch 2.0.1 (its own pin). The
# PyPI torch 2.0.1 wheel is the CUDA 11.7 build (INSTALL.md); the PyPI xformers 0.0.22 wheel is built for torch 2.0.1
# with CUDA 11.8 (sm_50-sm_90, no sm_86 / sm_89 SASS: the RTX 6000 Ada runs the sm_80 kernels).
